# HoloScript files

- `.holo` is the scene/composition syntax, `.hsplus` the typed semantic-component
  syntax (modules, templates, traits, reactive state, state machines), and `.hs` the
  logic syntax. Keep each file in its own surface.
- In `.holo`, prefer the modern `composition` / `template` / `object` pattern. The
  `orb` form is legacy: keep it working where it exists, but do not introduce it in
  new code.
- Names of compositions, templates and objects are double-quoted strings:
  `composition "Scene"`, `template "Enemy"`, `object "Crystal" using "Enemy"`.
- Traits are `@name` annotations, written before the properties of a template or
  after an object's name: `@grabbable @glowing`.
- Positions are three-number arrays: `position: [x, y, z]`.
- Only present syntax as valid when it matches an accepted example. The accepted
  grammar is defined by the parsers listed in
  `docs/spec/holoscript-grammar-ssot.md` in the HoloScript repository. Do not copy
  forms from `docs/language/holoscript-language-spec.md`, which that file marks as
  non-authoritative history.
- If you cannot tell whether a form parses, say so ("unknown") rather than guess.